From 3c7d931ec4b3d2335fcc06153139d05859f6a535 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:26:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ntr: the list memo: a display list seen before put into the
 record whole

A lean record frame's display lists made only of geometry (BEGIN / END,
the vertices, COLOR, NORMAL, TEXCOORD, NOP) and MTX_RESTORE are kept the
first time they run (their vertices, triangles, strip and the fields they
write) and replayed when the same words come with the same entry state:
only what the list reads before writing it, compared word for word (the
colour, texels and last vertex; the lighting and the restored slots'
direction matrices for a NORMAL; the texture matrix for texgen). Its
MTX_RESTOREs run again (this frame's matrices) and the matrix ids and
runs are made by the record's own steps. gx_list_begin names a list the
ROM DMAs in chunks. gx_list_memo(2) runs both ways and compares.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
